net neutrality part of the telecoms  package is meant to ensure that  broadband and mobile phone providers  give equal bandwidth for all internet  sites the new rules have divided the  left and the right but parliament's  rapporteur maintains that net neutrality  is safeguarded under the legislation  with this proposal we have reinforced  the openness of internets explain  that all traffic should be treated  equally independently of the center  independently of the the one that  received without discrimination without  interference but those who defend the  internet rights of citizens don't hold  the same view for example  orange  the package of reforms goes to plenary  in april  there are about 1.5 million posted  workers in europe they work on a  temporary basis in member states with  very little social protection and at the  same time the people that employ them  are getting cheap labor and taking the  business away from local businesses  that's why meps and the council have  reached an agreement and come up with an  eu director that better provides  protection for these posted workers and  makes it easier for member states to  monitor them the aim is to avoid any  attempt to circumvent the law the tax  has been defended by the employment  committee  there is the obligation for member  states to control a  hosting company there are a list of  control measures and also members say  they can establish new  control measures if this one which we  recommend today is not efficient if  adopted member states will then have  until 2016 to implement these rules
 

